{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
From Tirzah he went up the road
To [Bb]Samaria, with a [C]heavy load [Dm]
He struck down Shallum, son [C]of Ja[Dm]besh
And took [Bb]the throne for [C]himself, the [Dm]least
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Mena[Bb]hem son of [C]Gadi [Dm]reigned
In the [Bb]thir-ty-ninth [C]year, un[Dm]changed
He did [Bb]what was evil in [C]the Lord's [Dm]sight
Holding [Bb]power [C]by might and rite [Dm]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Tiphsah refused [C]to open its [Dm]gate
So he at[Bb]tacked, [C]sealing its [Dm]fate
He ripped open all the preg[C]nant wom[Dm]en
A brutal [Bb]end for their [C]broken [Dm]homes
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Mena[Bb]hem son of [C]Gadi [Dm]reigned
In the [Bb]thir-ty-ninth [C]year, un[Dm]changed
He did [Bb]what was evil in [C]the Lord's [Dm]sight
Holding [Bb]power by [C]might and [Dm]rite
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Pul [Bb]king of Assyria [C]came to the [Dm]land
Mena[Bb]hem paid the [C]silver de[Dm]mand
A thousand talents, heavy and cold
To keep the [Bb]Assyrian [C]forces [Dm]held
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Mena[Bb]hem son of [C]Gadi [Dm]reigned
In the [Bb]thir-ty-ninth [C]year, un[Dm]changed
He did [Bb]what was evil in [C]the Lord's [Dm]sight
Hold[Bb]ing power [C]by might and rite [Dm]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Fifty shekels from [C]every wealthy [Dm]man
[Bb]The king of Assyr[C]ia withdrew then [Dm]
Ten years [C]in Samaria [Dm]passed
In the [Bb]shad[C]ow of the [Dm]past
{end_of_verse}

